    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n95195" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκοτί-α</span></b> , ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκότος</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>darkness, gloom</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				4.1698
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				<u>Mi.</u>
				3.6
			</span></i>, al.), <u>NT</u> (<i><span class="en">
				<u>Ev.Matt.</u>
				10.27
			</span></i>, al.), cf. Moer.<i><span class="en">
				p.354
			</span></i> P. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> in
			Architecture, <i>scotia, cavetto</i>, a sunken moulding, so called
			from <i>the dark shadow</i> it casts, <i><span class="en">
				Vitr.
				3.5.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σκοτιά</span></b> , epith. of
			Aphrodite in Egypt, Id.</div>
